From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] tools/testing/modem_v1: SIPC5 ring vectors for the
 SS333 port (gate O2)

Host-side harness (make -C tools/testing/modem_v1 run) that compiles the
SIPC5 helpers (include/sipc5.h, include/circ_queue.h) and, extracted at
build time from the driver sources, sipc5_build_config/header() and
check_udl_space()/udl_write(), then checks the ring vectors of
loader_spec_v2.md section 10.4: header bytes, length fields, 4-byte
padding (the synthetic 921-byte frame takes 3 zero bytes, 928 in the
ring), the BOOT-over-SPI header strip, the 4/6-byte header boundary, the
decoding of a CP reply, and udl_write on a full-size ring, across a wrap
and in the all-or-nothing -ENOSPC case.  76 checks pass; with the 3.10
padding rule (sizeof(size_t)) a 64-bit host fails 20 of them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
